// Old Kettil, capercaillie, town-mother of Kettil's Rest (bible 3.4, character-bibles.md §8).
// Voice (style guide 4): proverbs, orders, laughter; counts people out loud; never says "Guild" without spitting.
// Her image: the count. Rooms: Rest_1 (the gate), Rest_2 (the square). State she reads: the count, Brann, the
// debate, the walk, Hollowvein, the unlicensed flag.

title: Rest_Kettil
---
<<if not has_flag("emberdown.kettil.met")>>
    <<jump Rest_Kettil_First>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("boss.brann.defeated") and not has_flag("emberdown.kettil.brann")>>
    Kettil: The crane's gone down the stair. Counted him out myself. One, gone. #line:02632ee
    Kettil: The furnace is cold for good. A town that can't be anchored by force. Remember that, Wren. #line:02acafc
    <<flag emberdown.kettil.brann 1>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.walked")>>
    Kettil: Thirty-one came up. We buried them in daylight. I counted every one, and I'll count them again tonight. #line:01d953c
<<elseif has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.buried")>>
    Kettil: The boards stay on. Some weights you carry by leaving them where they fell. #line:05717d3
<<elseif has_flag("emberdown.debate.heard") and walk_known() and not has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein_opened")>>
    <<jump Rest_Kettil_Hollowvein>>
<<else>>
    Kettil: Six hundred and eleven at supper. Six hundred and twelve with you. Eat something. #line:03857f4
<<endif>>
-> Who sings the roll-call? #line:033eaed
    Kettil: Runa. My voice went in the smoke. Hers came out of it louder. Up the bell stair. #line:0df9e44
-> What's under the boards at the pit-head? #line:009aba2
    Kettil: Hollowvein. Thirty-one of ours. Ask me again when you've heard the baths argue. #line:0260ec3
-> Nothing today. #line:0f27b53
    Kettil: Then go and be counted somewhere else. Ha. #line:049f956
===

title: Rest_Kettil_First
---
Kettil: Halt at the gate. One, two, and a stranger. You're the stranger. #line:0b163b4
Kettil: A stranger is a bird nobody remembers. Here, that's dangerous. For you, mostly. #line:05b57ef
<<if unlicensed()>>
    Kettil: And a cowl. A Guild cowl. She spits. Unlicensed, the reeds say. Better. Slightly. #line:0655ca5
<<else>>
    Kettil: And a cowl. A Guild cowl. She spits. Say you're not here to survey us. #line:0b9001b
<<endif>>
-> I'm here to go home. Halden. #line:0ba0e9c
    Kettil: Up the chimneys and over the ridge. Runa can teach you the wall. If she likes you. #line:05db8f8
-> The map sent me. #line:0e35f0e
    Kettil: Maps don't send. Birds with maps send. We know which ones. #line:0ced428
-> ... #line:0b629bf
    Kettil: Quiet. Good. The quiet ones get counted last and remembered longest. #line:00331dd
Kettil: Supper's at dusk. Roll-call after, at the bell. Be there and you're one of the count. #line:0000041
<<flag emberdown.kettil.met 1>>
===

title: Rest_Kettil_Hollowvein
---
Kettil: You heard the baths. You know the numbers. And the reeds say you know the walk. #line:0687313
Kettil: Thirty-one under the pit-head. Buried standing. The families want them up. #line:0c0c5c2
Kettil: I kept the boards on because what's down there broke the mine. #line:0fd3c2d
-> Then let's bring them up. #line:00621c3
    Kettil: Runa leads. You follow her count. Miss a name and you start the verse again. #line:0a5bd9c
    <<flag emberdown.hollowvein_opened 1>>
-> What broke the mine, Kettil? #line:0eb9b34
    Kettil: A stone that wouldn't stay still. It hums. Ask it yourself, at the bottom. #line:0b63e8f
    <<flag emberdown.hollowvein_opened 1>>
-> Leave the boards where they are. #line:0cf18b1
    Kettil: Aye. That's a count too. I'll tell the families you said it, not me. #line:0c00bfd
Kettil: The pit-head. Runa will be there before you. #line:06714c0
===
